    "title": "Paducah Christmas Parade 2025: Local Winners Announced and Event Video Available - NewsBreak",
    "text": "5 hours ago The City of Paducah held its annual Christmas Parade on December 6, 2025, in the downtown area. The theme was 'Sounds of Christmas.' More than 100 groups participated, featuring music and lights. Kentucky Supreme Court Justice Shea Nickell was the Grand Marshal. West Kentucky Community & Technical College’s production team recorded the event.\nWinners were recognized at the Paducah Board of Commissioners meeting on December 9. Darling Ingredients won for Themed Float. Washington Street Baptist Church won for Religious Float. Goodwin Farms won for Non-Float. Forest Friends won for School Float. Xplosive Force Dance Team 'XForce' won for Drill Team. Massac County High School Marching Patriots won for Band.\nVisit here for more details This post includes content assisted by AI tools. Please refer to the source for verification and additional information. Learn more.",
